explorer/
    Rome Protocol's own code, under LICENSE, except for the third-party parts listed here. The
    explorer uses three groups of them: npm packages, Rust crates compiled into WebAssembly, and fonts.

    npm packages, pinned exactly in explorer/package-lock.json and not copied into this repository.
    The pages are built from react, react-dom, scheduler, react-router, react-router-dom, cookie,
    set-cookie-parser, @tanstack/react-query and @tanstack/query-core, all MIT-licensed. The server
    runs with viem and the packages it depends on (@adraffy/ens-normalize,
    @noble/ciphers, @noble/curves, @noble/hashes, @scure/base, @scure/bip32, @scure/bip39, abitype,
    eventemitter3, isows, ox and ws), all MIT-licensed; they are installed from npm and not shipped
    with the pages. The build and test tools (Vite, Vitest, jsdom, Testing Library and their
    dependencies, under MIT, ISC, BSD-2-Clause, BSD-3-Clause, BlueOak-1.0.0, CC0-1.0, MIT-0, MPL-2.0
    for lightningcss, and Apache-2.0 for TypeScript and its native compiler packages, aria-query,
    detect-libc, expect-type and xml-name-validator) are not shipped with it.

